    "blurb": "SOAP web service integration",
    "overview": "Interact with SOAP-based web services directly within BPMN-based processes, enabling integration with legacy systems and enterprise services that rely on the SOAP protocol.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Integrate legacy systems with ease",
    "splashDescription": "The SOAP connector allows Camunda users to interact with SOAP-based web services directly within BPMN-based processes. It provides a configurable way to call operations defined in a Web Services Description Language (WSDL) file, enabling integration with legacy systems and enterprise services that rely on the SOAP protocol. This connector makes it easy to pass data to and from SOAP services, handle authentication, and parse responses streamlining interoperability between Camunda and external systems.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/565583/overview/img2971822995392944687.png?86391a2e993a42d60c5a9081d7238cf7",
